{
  "id": "COMPOUND:14682 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a consistent relationship between tris and Phosphodiesterase 6C, with multiple pathways linking tris to SNU1, which in turn is targeted by various compounds, including Diethylene glycol monolaurate, Fumiquinazoline K, and Trideca-3,5,7,9,11-pentayn-2-one. These compounds all share the common mechanism of targeting SNU1, which ultimately leads to the inhibition of Phosphodiesterase 6C. The high scores in all three paths indicate a strong, albeit indirect, connection between tris and Phosphodiesterase 6C, likely through the SNU1 intermediate. The recurring mechanism involves the interaction of tris with a target molecule that, in turn, modulates Phosphodiesterase 6C. This suggests that tris may act as a modulator or activator of the pathway leading to Phosphodiesterase 6C inhibition, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated.",
